        ],
        "observation": "Both actual screenshots personally viewed before this write. T.3 heading and baseline introduction are readable. At390 the fixed-header TOC circle is above body text; the old Windows/PowerShell/JSON wording and line ends have no floating body button. Inline paths wrap inside the body; at1280 separate TOC stays beside the text. Long code is inside its own horizontal scrolling container, not a page-wide overflow. No renewed VIS-001 at this original region."
      },
      {
        "recorded_after_personal_view_at": "2026-10-16T21:02:15.312712+00:00",
        "screenshot_ids": [
          "1280-T2-history",
          "390-T2-history",
          "390-T8-baseline"
        ],
        "observation": "Personally viewed all three before recording. T.2 parenthesis and all five field rows remain readable at both widths; effective_tokens wraps across a code word on390 but every letter is visible and the role row remains paired. The paragraph makes history-first-record location explicit without changing dry-run meaning. Mobile T.8 heading, LayerNorm/RMS/MoE roles and baseline32-width explanation remain readable; four command lines stay in their local code viewport. Fixed-header control does not obscure either body region."
      },
      {
        "recorded_after_personal_view_at": "2026-10-16T21:02:37.376603+00:00",
        "screenshot_ids": [
          "1280-T8-baseline",
          "390-T8-code-right",
          "1280-T10-teachers",
          "390-T10-teachers"
        ],
        "observation": "Personally viewed before this record. T.8 desktop shows separate unmodified baseline, rms and moe command rows and comparison limits; mobile horizontal scrolling exposes baseline.pt/rms.pt/moe.pt ends without pushing body off-screen. T.10 teacher table has all three teacher/model/data columns at both widths; mobile filenames wrap into visible contiguous pieces rather than disappear. Table and surrounding preparation/limited-GSM8K wording are readable. No body-overlapping TOC control."
      },
      {
        "recorded_after_personal_view_at": "2026-10-16T21:02:59.582118+00:00",
